// Hot swap in the REPL break loop: what works today of the break-loop
// milestone (`break_loop.transcript` is the fuller target).
//
// `raymarch.loko`'s `shade` method produces a negative brightness for rays
// that miss the sphere, and `check-sample` signals `<bad-sample>`, which
// nothing handles. The run stops with every frame live. Fixing `shade`
// compiles the session again and installs it as a new code unit (`u1`)
// beside the running one (`u0`): only the `shade` frame runs code the edit
// replaced. `retry frame:1` unwinds to the `shade` call and makes it again
// with the new method, so `main` returns 1.0 + 0.5 + 0.0 while `pixel`,
// `render` and `main` finish on the code they started with. A new run takes
// the new code from the start.
//
// Format: see `tests/support/transcript.rs`.

=== repl: edit a method under a suspended signal and retry its frame

> :load tests/fixtures/break_loop/raymarch.loko
loaded tests/fixtures/break_loop/raymarch.loko (10 forms)
> :run main
break [1]: no handler for <bad-sample>; 6 frames suspended, nothing unwound
frames (innermost first):
  frame:0 check-sample  u0:f0
  frame:1 shade#method0  u0:f4
  frame:2 shade#dispatch  u0:f9
  frame:3 pixel  u0:f1
  frame:4 render  u0:f2
  frame:5 main  u0:f3
restarts:
  restart:0 skip-pixel()  the handle site's recovery
  restart:1 use-value(<double-float>)  the signal returns the value
  restart:2 retry(frame)  call a frame's function again, with current definitions
  restart:3 abort()  unwind to top level, running cleanups
choose with :restart <n|name> [args...], or :edit <form-id> to fix a definition

// A broken edit is rejected and changes nothing; the fixed one installs.
> :edit form:f6
editing form:f6; enter a replacement definition
> define method shade(s :: <sphere>, distance :: <double-float>) => <double-float>
>   // A ray that misses the sphere is black, not negatively bright.
>   check-sample(max(0, 1.0 - distance / s.radius), distance)
> end;
! diagnostics:
!   Error sem.function-argument-type-mismatch 1091..1092 function `max` argument 1 expects <float> but got <integer>
! edit rejected; the definitions and break [1] are unchanged
> define method shade(s :: <sphere>, distance :: <double-float>) => <double-float>
>   // A ray that misses the sphere is black, not negatively bright.
>   check-sample(max(0.0, 1.0 - distance / s.radius), distance)
> end;
installed the edit as a new code unit; still running replaced code:
  frame:1 shade#method0  u0:f4  superseded by u1:f4
> :frames
frames (innermost first):
  frame:0 check-sample  u0:f0
  frame:1 shade#method0  u0:f4  superseded by u1:f4
  frame:2 shade#dispatch  u0:f9
  frame:3 pixel  u0:f1
  frame:4 render  u0:f2
  frame:5 main  u0:f3

// Retry the shade frame with the new method: 1.0 + 0.5 + 0.0.
> :restart retry frame:1
1.5
> :run main
1.5

// Bring the bug back, then resume the signal with a typed value:
// 1.0 + 0.5 + 0.25. A string is refused and the break keeps waiting.
